// C primitive: on a grammar declaration, @defaults(m) makes every declaration
// of that kind apply @m unless it writes @m itself; the macro's target type
// selects which @m. The implicit application is not listed in the
// declaration's #macros, so @m can tell a default application from a written
// one. C attaches it when the declaration joins the graph.
@builtin
macro defaults(let applies: Macro): Construct
